 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? That's common with Shimano chain. You can try lubing it with very little oil and little cotton to see if that stops it. Use a clean finger instead of wiping with cloth, and only a few drafts. If it works after few miles, you've found the solution. Drabble the chain into each gear, then spin the pedal slowly between each one. application at the ends, and let the excess fall down off by fingers. Clean it first with mild soap if it' dirty. For a squeak, yes. If it were really dirty, go straight to cleaning and lubing.",
